  "configuration_id": "config_036",
  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is RNA-only multiprofile with scvi_n200, reaching about 0.65 accuracy and 0.63 F1, while image-only multiprofile avgpool is much weaker, with imagenet_vit_l slightly better than resnet50 in both accuracy and F1. No multimodal configuration has been tested yet. config_036 keeps the known strong RNA setting (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) and the slightly better known image setting (imagenet_vit_l, multiprofile, avgpool), then tests the simplest fusion rule, concat. This directly clarifies whether adding image information via concat improves over the strong RNA-only baseline without confounding the result with untested transformer image aggregation or a more complex weighted fusion. It is the best next experiment because it exploits the strongest RNA evidence while establishing a clean multimodal baseline before exploring transformer aggregation or weighted fusion."
}

